# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Upload the workflow, and pass the name of the backend when you run it:\n"
msgstr "Unggah workflow-nya, lalu kirim nama Backend saat menjalankannya:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "After the job ends, get the IDs of the workflow's QPU jobs from the managed workflow job:\n"
msgstr "Setelah job selesai, ambil ID job QPU milik workflow dari job managed workflow:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Each ID is a regular primitive job ID. To read a job's status and results, see [Retrieve job results at a later time](/guides/monitor-job#retrieve-job-results-at-a-later-time).\n"
"If the workflow ran primitives in a session or batch, list the session and batch IDs with `runtime_sessions()`, and pass one to `runtime_jobs()` to get only the jobs in it:\n"
msgstr ""
"Setiap ID adalah ID job primitive biasa. Untuk membaca status dan hasil sebuah job, lihat [Ambil hasil job di lain waktu](/guides/monitor-job#retrieve-job-results-at-a-later-time).\n"
"Kalau workflow menjalankan primitive di Session atau batch, daftarkan ID Session dan batch dengan `runtime_sessions()`, lalu kirim salah satunya ke `runtime_jobs()` untuk mendapatkan job di dalamnya saja:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "**`run_workflow_remotely.ipynb`**\n"
msgstr "**`run_workflow_remotely.ipynb`**\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The `job` object exists only in the notebook that started the run. In a new notebook, get the job again with `client.job(\"<your-job-id>\")`, then call `runtime_jobs()` on it. See [Find a job from a new session](/guides/run-managed-workflow#find-a-job-from-a-new-session).\n"
msgstr "Objek `job` hanya ada di notebook yang memulai run. Di notebook baru, ambil job-nya lagi dengan `client.job(\"<your-job-id>\")`, lalu panggil `runtime_jobs()` di atasnya. Lihat [Temukan job dari Session baru](/guides/run-managed-workflow#find-a-job-from-a-new-session).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "For the QPU usage and run times of each QPU job, see [View job metrics](/guides/monitor-job#view-job-metrics). For the usage of your whole instance in the current period, call `client.usage()`. To see how long each stage of the managed workflow job took, see [Check how long each stage took](/guides/run-managed-workflow#check-how-long-each-stage-took).\n"
msgstr "Untuk penggunaan QPU dan waktu run tiap job QPU, lihat [Lihat metrik job](/guides/monitor-job#view-job-metrics). Untuk penggunaan seluruh instance kamu di periode saat ini, panggil `client.usage()`. Untuk melihat berapa lama setiap tahapan job managed workflow berlangsung, lihat [Cek berapa lama setiap tahapan berlangsung](/guides/run-managed-workflow#check-how-long-each-stage-took).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Cancel linked QPU jobs {#cancel-linked-qpu-jobs}"
msgstr "Batalkan job QPU yang terhubung {#cancel-linked-qpu-jobs}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "When you cancel a managed workflow job with `job.cancel()`, the workflow also tries to cancel the QPU work that the workflow started:\n"
msgstr "Saat kamu membatalkan job managed workflow dengan `job.cancel()`, workflow juga mencoba membatalkan pekerjaan QPU yang dimulainya:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Sessions and batches.** The workflow cancels each of the workflow's sessions and batches, which also cancels their queued jobs.\n"
msgstr "**Session dan batch.** Workflow membatalkan setiap Session dan batch miliknya, yang juga membatalkan job mereka yang masih antre.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Other primitive jobs.** The workflow cancels each of the workflow's other primitive jobs that are still queued or running.\n"
msgstr "**Job primitive lainnya.** Workflow membatalkan setiap job primitive lain miliknya yang masih antre atau berjalan.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "`job.cancel()` returns a message for each QPU job and session, so you can check what was canceled:\n"
msgstr "`job.cancel()` mengembalikan pesan untuk setiap job QPU dan Session, jadi kamu bisa cek apa saja yang dibatalkan:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "For a workflow that ran in a batch, the message looks like the following:\n"
msgstr "Untuk workflow yang berjalan di batch, pesannya terlihat seperti berikut:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "If the client cannot create a `QiskitRuntimeService` from your local credentials, it cancels only the managed workflow job. Cancel the QPU jobs yourself with their IDs from `job.runtime_jobs()`.\n"
msgstr "Kalau klien tidak bisa membuat `QiskitRuntimeService` dari kredensial lokal kamu, klien hanya membatalkan job managed workflow. Batalkan sendiri job QPU-nya dengan ID dari `job.runtime_jobs()`.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "When a workflow stops a job itself, for example because it reached the 24-hour limit, it does not cancel its QPU jobs. Cancel them with their IDs from `job.runtime_jobs()`.\n"
msgstr "Saat workflow menghentikan job sendiri, misalnya karena mencapai batas 24 jam, workflow tidak membatalkan job QPU-nya. Batalkan dengan ID dari `job.runtime_jobs()`.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "{/* REVIEW: the scheduler's timeout and blocked-account stops (update_fleets_jobs_statuses.py stop_job_if_timeout, FleetsJobCanceller) cancel only the fleet. Only the user stop endpoint (StopJobUseCase) cancels runtime jobs. Confirm whether this is intended before publishing. */}\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Troubleshoot QPU jobs in a workflow {#troubleshoot-qpu-jobs-in-a-workflow}"
msgstr "Atasi masalah job QPU di workflow {#troubleshoot-qpu-jobs-in-a-workflow}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Problem | Cause |\n"
"| - | - |\n"
"| `get_runtime_service()` raises `KeyError: 'QISKIT_IBM_CHANNEL'`. | The code runs in your local notebook, not in a managed workflow job. Use `QiskitRuntimeService()` locally. |\n"
"| `update_status()` returns `False`, and the logs show `'sub_status' not provided or is not valid`. | The value is not one of the `Job` constants, or the job is no longer active. |\n"
"| `job.runtime_jobs()` returns `[]`. | The workflow created its service with `QiskitRuntimeService()`, or it has not run a primitive yet. |\n"
"| A session's jobs are not tracked. | The session was created from a backend of a different service. Get the backend from `get_runtime_service()`. |\n"
"| The workflow logs show `Could not associate runtime job with serverless job`. | The workflow could not record a primitive job. The primitive job still runs, but it is not tracked. |\n"
"| `job.cancel()` shows `No QiskitRuntimeService can be associated to the given token and instance.` | The client could not create a `QiskitRuntimeService` from your local credentials, so it canceled only the managed workflow job. |\n"
"| `client.job()` fails with `Job [...] not found`. | The job ID is wrong, or the job belongs to another user. |\n"
msgstr ""
"| Masalah | Penyebab |\n"
"| - | - |\n"
"| `get_runtime_service()` memunculkan `KeyError: 'QISKIT_IBM_CHANNEL'`. | Kode berjalan di notebook lokal kamu, bukan di job managed workflow. Pakai `QiskitRuntimeService()` secara lokal. |\n"
"| `update_status()` mengembalikan `False`, dan log menampilkan `'sub_status' not provided or is not valid`. | Nilainya bukan salah satu konstanta `Job`, atau job sudah tidak aktif. |\n"
"| `job.runtime_jobs()` mengembalikan `[]`. | Workflow membuat service-nya dengan `QiskitRuntimeService()`, atau belum menjalankan primitive. |\n"
"| Job milik sebuah Session tidak terlacak. | Session dibuat dari Backend milik service yang berbeda. Ambil Backend dari `get_runtime_service()`. |\n"
"| Log workflow menampilkan `Could not associate runtime job with serverless job`. | Workflow tidak bisa mencatat sebuah job primitive. Job primitive-nya tetap berjalan, tapi tidak terlacak. |\n"
"| `job.cancel()` menampilkan `No QiskitRuntimeService can be associated to the given token and instance.` | Klien tidak bisa membuat `QiskitRuntimeService` dari kredensial lokal kamu, jadi hanya job managed workflow yang dibatalkan. |\n"
"| `client.job()` gagal dengan `Job [...] not found`. | ID job salah, atau job milik pengguna lain. |\n"

